Below is a quick “road‑map” of the columns that look useful for each requirement, the main filters you will probably need, followed by ten exploratory / prototype BigQuery statements (each limited to 20 rows, all wrapped in ```sql``` with an explanatory comment).

────────────────────────────────────────
RELEVANT COLUMNS & POSSIBLE FILTERS
────────────────────────────────────────
mbb_teams
  • venue_name          :   the building’s name
  • market, name        :   school & team names (to form “Venue” label)
  • venue_capacity      :   seats available  → sort desc for “Top Venues”
  • venue_city/state    :   optional context  

mbb_games_sr
  • season              :   season filter ( >2015 for champs, >2010 otherwise)
  • scheduled_date      :   game date for output
  • tournament_round    :   look for values such as “National Championship”
  • h_market / h_name   :   home school + nickname
  • a_market / a_name   :   away school + nickname
  • h_points / a_points :   points scored → (h_points+a_points) & |h_pts-a_pts|
  • h_three_points_made / a_three_points_made :   threes made → sum
  • venue_capacity / venue_name               :   per‑game capacity if you prefer

Main conditions likely used
  – Top Venues : ORDER BY venue_capacity DESC
  – Big Champ Margins : season > 2015 AND LOWER(tournament_round) LIKE '%championship%'
  – Highest Scoring Games : season > 2010  ORDER BY (h_points+a_points) DESC
  – Total Threes : season > 2010  ORDER BY (h_three_points_made+a_three_points_made) DESC

────────────────────────────────────────
10 STEP‑BY‑STEP / INCREASINGLY COMPLEX QUERIES
────────────────────────────────────────
```sql
-- 1. List distinct tournament rounds to see the exact wording of the championship flag
SELECT DISTINCT tournament_round
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE tournament_round IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Peek at recent seasons’ championship games (season > 2015)
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       h_market||' vs '||a_market AS matchup,
       h_points, a_points, (h_points - a_points) AS margin
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2015
  AND LOWER(tournament_round) LIKE '%championship%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect total points for games since 2011, highest first
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       h_market||' vs '||a_market AS matchup,
       (h_points + a_points) AS total_pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2010
ORDER BY total_pts DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect total three‑pointers made in games since 2011
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       h_market||' vs '||a_market AS matchup,
       (h_three_points_made + a_three_points_made) AS combined_threes
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2010
ORDER BY combined_threes DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Check which teams report the biggest arenas in mbb_teams
SELECT market AS school,
       venue_name,
       venue_capacity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_teams`
WHERE venue_capacity IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY venue_capacity DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Verify that three‑pointer fields are present & non‑null
SELECT COUNT(*) AS non_null_games
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2010
  AND h_three_points_made IS NOT NULL
  AND a_three_points_made IS NOT NULL;
```

```sql
-- 7. Build champion‑margin list with explicit key metric (abs margin)
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       CONCAT(h_market,' vs ',a_market) AS matchup,
       ABS(h_points - a_points) AS abs_margin
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2015
  AND LOWER(tournament_round) LIKE '%championship%'
ORDER BY abs_margin DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but restrict to National Championship *and* filter out women/other tourneys if needed
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       CONCAT(h_market,' vs ',a_market) AS matchup,
       ABS(h_points - a_points) AS abs_margin
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2015
  AND LOWER(tournament) LIKE '%ncaa%'
  AND LOWER(tournament_round) LIKE '%championship%'
ORDER BY abs_margin DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Top venues again but grouping (if same building appears for multiple schools)
SELECT venue_name,
       MAX(venue_capacity) AS seats
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_teams`
WHERE venue_capacity IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY venue_name
ORDER BY seats DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Prototype of the final UNION ALL table (top 5 each category)
--    ⚠️  This is just to illustrate structure; refine ORDER BY & LIMIT per sub‑query.
SELECT 'Top Venues'            AS Category,
       'N/A'                   AS Date,
       venue_name              AS `Matchup or Venue`,
       CAST(venue_capacity AS STRING) AS `Key Metric`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_teams`
WHERE venue_capacity IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY venue_capacity DESC
LIMIT 5

UNION ALL

SELECT 'Biggest Championship Margins',
       CAST(scheduled_date AS STRING),
       CONCAT(h_market,' ',h_name,' vs ',a_market,' ',a_name),
       CAST(ABS(h_points - a_points) AS STRING)
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2015
  AND LOWER(tournament_round) LIKE '%championship%'
ORDER BY ABS(h_points - a_points) DESC
LIMIT 5

UNION ALL

SELECT 'Highest Scoring Games',
       CAST(scheduled_date AS STRING),
       CONCAT(h_market,' ',h_name,' vs ',a_market,' ',a_name),
       CAST((h_points + a_points) AS STRING)
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2010
ORDER BY (h_points + a_points) DESC
LIMIT 5

UNION ALL

SELECT 'Total Threes',
       CAST(scheduled_date AS STRING),
       CONCAT(h_market,' ',h_name,' vs ',a_market,' ',a_name),
       CAST((h_three_points_made + a_three_points_made) AS STRING)
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE season > 2010
  AND h_three_points_made IS NOT NULL
  AND a_three_points_made IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY (h_three_points_made + a_three_points_made) DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

The ten snippets above gradually explore each needed component and culminate in a single UNION ALL query that already produces the requested four‑section table (with the Date field set to “N/A” for the venue rows). Tune string concatenations and filter wording if inspection queries (#1‑#4) reveal slightly different text values in the raw data.
